DEV_VERSION=13
RERELEASE=1
DESCRIPTION=FL-02 stage 2, part 1: the freestanding image's bss moves above 1 MiB. linker.ld links .bss at FL_KERNEL_BSS_ADDR (0x100000) and never loads it, so only code, read-only data and data stay below 0x9f000: the loaded image now ends at 0x82118 (0x86160 for the security lab), leaving about 115 KiB (99 KiB) of conventional memory for the KeyQuorum checkpoints. Stage 2 refuses a bss end outside the identity map and refuses to boot unless one usable E820 entry holds the whole bss (FLINTSTONE_BOOT_FAIL bss-memory), since entry.asm zeroes it before any C check; the boot info reserves the image and the bss as two ranges, so the KeyQuorum heap starts past the bss. fl_bootinfo_validate takes the image end and checks both ranges and the bss against the E820 map, reading the map only after its address is known not to wrap. The build script and the browser-lab workflow check the image end against the budget and the bss start; build-info.json gains imageEnd and bssStart. test_fs_bootmap covers the new refusals, and the QEMU shell and entry tests pass.
